files have been added to the project.\n\nThe first one, `.gitignore`, excludes the `.idea` directory, which typically contains IDE-specific settings for JetBrains IDEs like IntelliJ IDEA or PyCharm. Excluding this directory is a good practice as it prevents team members from having to deal with potentially conflicting IDE configurations.\n\nThe second one, `frontend/static/.gitignore`, excludes the `/dist` directory within the `frontend/static` folder. This suggests that `/dist` likely contains the build output (e.g., bundled JavaScript, compiled CSS, etc.) of a frontend application. It''s common to exclude build artifacts from version control as they can be regenerated and would otherwise bloat the repository.","tree":{"sha":"d0521d6b82f4e872b22b8cbc5ae8f139f2e25fec","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/git/trees/d0521d6b82f4e872b22b8cbc5ae8f139f2e25fec"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/git/commits/dcea5117766e4170deefaa122125402a7ed86a7e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3142325?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ddenysov","id":3142325,"login":"ddenysov","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxNDIzMjU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ddenysov/canope/commit/dcea5117766e4170deefaa122125402a7ed86a7e","node_id":"C_kwDOO2zci9oAKGRjZWE1MTE3NzY2ZTQxNzBkZWVmYWExMjIxMjU0MDJhN2VkODZhN2U","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ddenysov/canope/commit/cd7462dac0150461f992ae31ff4bdd857c2b44cd","sha":"cd7462dac0150461f992ae31ff4bdd857c2b44cd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/commits/cd7462dac0150461f992ae31ff4bdd857c2b44cd"}],"sha":"dcea5117766e4170deefaa122125402a7ed86a7e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/commits/dcea5117766e4170deefaa122125402a7ed86a7e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3142325?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ddenysov","id":3142325,"login":"ddenysov","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxNDIzMjU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/commits/cd7462dac0150461f992ae31ff4bdd857c2b44cd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-06-25T09:31:17Z","email":"denisov1985@gmail.com","name":"Dmytro Denysov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-06-25T09:31:17Z","email":"denisov1985@gmail.com","name":"Dmytro Denysov"},"message":"```\nIndex: frontend/sign_up/.gitignore\n===================================================================\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/frontend/sign_up/.gitignore\n@@ -0,0 +1,30 @@\n+# Logs\n+logs\n+*.log\n+npm-debug.log*\n+yarn-debug.log*\n+yarn-error.log*\n+pnpm-debug.log*\n+lerna-debug.log*\n+\n+node_modules\n+.DS_Store\n+dist\n+dist-ssr\n+coverage\n+*.local\n+\n+/cypress/videos/\n+/cypress/screenshots/\n+\n+# Editor directories and files\n+.vscode/*\n+!.vscode/extensions.json\n+.idea\n+*.suo\n+*.ntvs*\n+*.njsproj\n+*.sln\n+*.sw?\n+\n+*.tsbuildinfo\n```\n\nThe `.gitignore` file in the `frontend/sign_up` directory specifies intentionally untracked files that Git should ignore. This includes logs, dependency directories, build outputs, local environment-specific files, Cypress test results, and editor-specific settings.\n\n```\nIndex: frontend/sign_up/.prettierrc.json\n===================================================================\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/frontend/sign_up/.prettierrc.json\n@@ -0,0 +1,6 @@\n+{\n+  \"$schema\": \"https://json.schemastore.org/prettierrc\",\n+  \"semi\": false,\n+  \"singleQuote\": true,\n+  \"printWidth\": 100\n+}\n```\n\nThe `.prettierrc.json` file in the `frontend/sign_up` directory configures Prettier, a code formatter, with the following settings:\n\n- `$schema`: Specifies the schema for the configuration file, enabling autocompletion and validation in supported editors.\n- `semi`: Sets whether semicolons should be added at the end of statements (`false` means no semicolons).\n- `singleQuote`: Sets whether to use single quotes instead of double quotes for strings (`true` means use single quotes).\n- `printWidth`: Sets the maximum line length before wrapping (`100` characters).\n\n```\nIndex: frontend/sign_up/.gitattributes\n===================================================================\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/frontend/sign_up/.gitattributes\n@@ -0,0 +1,1 @@\n+* text=auto eol=lf\n```\n\nThe `.gitattributes` file in the `frontend/sign_up` directory defines attributes for files in the repository, specifically:\n\n- `* text=auto eol=lf`:  This sets the default text attribute to `auto` for all files, allowing Git to handle end-of-line characters automatically. It also ensures that line endings are converted to Line Feed (`lf`) on checkout, promoting consistency across different operating systems.\n\n```\nIndex: frontend/sign_up/tsconfig.json\n===================================================================\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/frontend/sign_up/tsconfig.json\n@@ -0,0 +1,14 @@\n+{\n+  \"files\": [],\n+  \"references\": [\n+    {\n+      \"path\": \"./tsconfig.node.json\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"path\": \"./tsconfig.app.json\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"path\": \"./tsconfig.vitest.json\"\n+    }\n+  ]\n+}\n```\n\nThe `tsconfig.json` file in the `frontend/sign_up` directory serves as the main TypeScript configuration file for the project. It uses the \"references\" property to include other TypeScript configuration files, allowing for a modular and organized project structure. Specifically, it includes configurations for node-related files (`tsconfig.node.json`), application-specific files (`tsconfig.app.json`), and Vitest-related files (`tsconfig.vitest.json`).  This promotes a clear separation of concerns within the TypeScript build process.\n\n```\nIndex: frontend/sign_up/tsconfig.vitest.json\n===================================================================\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/frontend/sign_up/tsconfig.vitest.json\n@@ -0,0 +1,11 @@\n+{\n+  \"extends\": \"./tsconfig.app.json\",\n+  \"include\": [\"src/**/__tests__/*\", \"env.d.ts\"],\n+  \"exclude\": [],\n+  \"compilerOptions\": {\n+    \"tsBuildInfoFile\": \"./node_modules/.tmp/tsconfig.vitest.tsbuildinfo\",\n+\n+    \"lib\": [],\n+    \"types\": [\"node\", \"jsdom\"]\n+  }\n+}\n```\n\nThe `tsconfig.vitest.json` file in `frontend/sign_up` provides TypeScript configuration specifically for Vitest unit testing. It extends the application''s base configuration (`tsconfig.app.json`), includes test files (`src/**/__tests__/*`) and type definitions (`env.d.ts`), excludes no files, and sets compiler options.  The `tsBuildInfoFile` specifies a separate build info file for Vitest. `lib` is set to an empty array, indicating no specific libraries are included beyond those inherited from the base config. `types` includes \"node\" and \"jsdom\" to provide type checking for Node.js and the jsdom testing environment.\n\n```\nIndex: frontend/sign_up/vitest.config.ts\n===================================================================\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/frontend/sign_up/vitest.config.ts\n@@ -0,0 +1,14 @@\n+import { fileURLToPath } from ''node:url''\n+import { mergeConfig, defineConfig, configDefaults } from ''vitest/config''\n+import viteConfig from ''./vite.config''\n+\n+export default mergeConfig(\n+  viteConfig,\n+  defineConfig({\n+    test: {\n+      environment: ''jsdom'',\n+      exclude: [...configDefaults.exclude, ''e2e/**''],\n+      root: fileURLToPath(new URL(''./'', import.meta.url)),\n+    },\n+  }),\n+)\n```\n\nThe `vitest.config.ts` file in the `frontend/sign_up` directory configures Vitest, a testing framework, by merging settings with the Vite configuration (`vite.config.ts`). The test environment is set to `jsdom` to simulate a browser environment. It excludes end-to-end tests (`e2e/**`) and sets the root directory for tests to the current directory.\n\n```\nIndex: frontend/sign_up/src/main.ts\n===================================================================\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/frontend/sign_up/src/main.ts\n@@ -0,0 +1,9 @@\n+import { createApp } from ''vue''\n+import { createPinia } from ''pinia''\n+import SignUp from ''./SignUp.vue''\n+\n+const app = createApp(SignUp)\n+\n+app.use(createPinia())\n+\n+app.mount(''#app'')\n```\n\nThe `src/main.ts` file in `frontend/sign_up` is the entry point for the Vue.js application. It creates a Vue application instance using `SignUp.vue` as the root component. It also sets up Pinia for state management and mounts the 