ll,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3142325?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ddenysov","id":3142325,"login":"ddenysov","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxNDIzMjU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ddenysov/canope/commit/c0634fa24d3c9f7133846c10bd2d8a3e12b3f76e","node_id":"C_kwDOO2zci9oAKGMwNjM0ZmEyNGQzYzlmNzEzMzg0NmMxMGJkMmQ4YTNlMTJiM2Y3NmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ddenysov/canope/commit/0663f2b903491e56bb08117ef3f71d77e97fe879","sha":"0663f2b903491e56bb08117ef3f71d77e97fe879","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/commits/0663f2b903491e56bb08117ef3f71d77e97fe879"}],"sha":"c0634fa24d3c9f7133846c10bd2d8a3e12b3f76e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/commits/c0634fa24d3c9f7133846c10bd2d8a3e12b3f76e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3142325?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ddenysov","id":3142325,"login":"ddenysov","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxNDIzMjU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/commits/0663f2b903491e56bb08117ef3f71d77e97fe879/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-06-22T12:26:16Z","email":"denisov1985@gmail.com","name":"Dmytro Denysov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-06-22T12:26:16Z","email":"denisov1985@gmail.com","name":"Dmytro Denysov"},"message":"Okay, I''ve analyzed the changes and here''s a summary:\n\n**Overall**:  The changes represent a shift from a standard Vue CLI project structure to a module federation setup using Webpack. It involves removing the original Vue CLI project files and introducing new configurations and components tailored for module federation.\n\n**Key Changes:**\n\n*   **Project Structure:** The original Vue CLI project (`frontend/vue-cli/vue-project/`) is being replaced with a new structure that includes separate projects for `host` and `ui` (likely representing the main application and a shared component library, respectively).\n*   **Build System:**  The project transitions from using Vue CLI''s built-in build system (based on Webpack) to explicit `webpack.config.js` files for each project (`host` and `ui`).\n*   **Module Federation:** The core of the changes is the introduction of Webpack''s Module Federation plugin. This is evident in the `webpack.config.js` files, where `ModuleFederationPlugin` is used to define remotes, exposes, and shared dependencies.\n*   **Component Sharing:** The `ui` project is configured to expose components (like `UiButton`) for use in other federated modules (like the `host` and `sign_up` projects).\n*   **Remote Loading:** The `host` project and sign\\_up project are set up to consume remote modules, specifically the components exposed by the `ui` project. The sign\\_up project also imports ui.\n*   **PrimeVue Integration**: Both ui and sign\\_up projects include PrimeVue and a theme\n*   **Vue Composition API:** The code uses the Vue 3 Composition API (`<script setup>`) for component logic.\n*   **HTML Templates:** The `index.html` is now directly managed in the webpack config in both ui and host project configs.\n*   **Dependencies:** New dependencies are added, including:\n    *   `@primeuix/themes`\n    *   `primevue`\n    *   `webpack-dev-server`\n\n**Removed Files:**\n\n*   A lot of standard Vue CLI project files are being deleted such as `.editorconfig`, `.gitignore`, `.prettierrc.json`, `src/*`, `public/*`, `env.d.ts`, `eslint.config.ts`, `.vscode/extensions.json`, `index.html`, `tsconfig.*.json`, and `vite.config.ts`.\n\n**New Files:**\n\n*   `frontend/ui/.gitignore`\n*   `frontend/ui/src/main.js`\n*   `frontend/ui/src/App.vue`\n*   `frontend/ui/webpack.config.js`\n*   `frontend/host/src/components/SignUp.vue`\n\nLet me know if you''d like a deeper dive into any specific aspect of these changes!","tree":{"sha":"585fed19cc87a41cd59cef728ed27425180fcc68","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/git/trees/585fed19cc87a41cd59cef728ed27425180fcc68"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/git/commits/0663f2b903491e56bb08117ef3f71d77e97fe879","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3142325?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ddenysov","id":3142325,"login":"ddenysov","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxNDIzMjU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ddenysov/canope/commit/0663f2b903491e56bb08117ef3f71d77e97fe879","node_id":"C_kwDOO2zci9oAKDA2NjNmMmI5MDM0OTFlNTZiYjA4MTE3ZWYzZjcxZDc3ZTk3ZmU4Nzk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ddenysov/canope/commit/fa54edfdd0e7a878f0d3dec25f869a895e19896b","sha":"fa54edfdd0e7a878f0d3dec25f869a895e19896b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/commits/fa54edfdd0e7a878f0d3dec25f869a895e19896b"}],"sha":"0663f2b903491e56bb08117ef3f71d77e97fe879","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/commits/0663f2b903491e56bb08117ef3f71d77e97fe879"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3142325?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ddenysov","id":3142325,"login":"ddenysov","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxNDIzMjU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/commits/fa54edfdd0e7a878f0d3dec25f869a895e19896b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-06-22T12:21:28Z","email":"denisov1985@gmail.com","name":"Dmytro Denysov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-06-22T12:21:28Z","email":"denisov1985@gmail.com","name":"Dmytro Denysov"},"message":"Okay, I''ve analyzed the changes and here''s a summary:\n\n**Overall**:  The changes represent a shift from a standard Vue CLI project structure to a module federation setup using Webpack. It involves removing the original Vue CLI project files and introducing new configurations and components tailored for module federation.\n\n**Key Changes:**\n\n*   **Project Structure:** The original Vue CLI project (`frontend/vue-cli/vue-project/`) is being replaced with a new structure that includes separate projects for `host` and `ui` (likely representing the main application and a shared component library, respectively).\n*   **Build System:**  The project transitions from using Vue CLI''s built-in build system (based on Webpack) to explicit `webpack.config.js` files for each project (`host` and `ui`).\n*   **Module Federation:** The core of the changes is the introduction of Webpack''s Module Federation plugin. This is evident in the `webpack.config.js` files, where `ModuleFederationPlugin` is used to define remotes, exposes, and shared dependencies.\n*   **Component Sharing:** The `ui` project is configured to expose components (like `UiButton`) for use in other federated modules (like the `host` and `sign_up` projects).\n*   **Remote Loading:** The `host` project and sign\\_up project are set up to consume remote modules, specifically the components exposed by the `ui` project. The sign\\_up project also imports ui.\n*   **PrimeVue Integration**: Both ui and sign\\_up projects include PrimeVue and a theme\n*   **Vue Composition API:** The code uses the Vue 3 Composition API (`<script setup>`) for component logic.\n*   **HTML Templates:** The `index.html` is now directly managed in the webpack config in both ui and host project configs.\n*   **Dependencies:** New dependencies are added, including:\n    *   `@primeuix/themes`\n    *   `primevue`\n    *   `webpack-dev-server`\n\n**Removed Files:**\n\n*   A lot of standard Vue CLI project files are being deleted such as `.editorconfig`, `.gitignore`, `.prettierrc.json`, `src/*`, `public/*`, `env.d.ts`, `eslint.config.ts`, `.vscode/extensions.json`, `index.html`, `tsconfig.*.json`, and `vite.config.ts`.\n\n**New Files:**\n\n*   `frontend/ui/.gitignore`\n*   `frontend/ui/src/main.js`\n*   `frontend/ui/src/App.vue`\n*   `frontend/ui/webpack.config.js`\n*   `frontend/host/src/components/SignUp.vue`\n\nLet me know if you''d like a deeper dive into any specific aspect of these changes!","tree":{"sha":"fae41e31e03078cbeb2e53cac6878c0270404886","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/git/trees/fae41e31e03078cbeb2e53cac6878c0270404886"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/git/commits/fa54edfdd0e7a878f0d3dec25f869a895e19896b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3142325?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ddenysov","id":3142325,"login":"ddenysov","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxNDIzMjU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ddenysov/canope/commit/fa54edfdd0e7a878f0d3dec25f869a895e19896b","node_id":"C_kwDOO2zci9oAKGZhNTRlZGZkZDBlN2E4NzhmMGQzZGVjMjVmODY5YTg5NWUxOTg5NmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ddenysov/canope/commit/2e1c6cc11891904b46ace0a7895d0d167d9bf5ce","sha":"2e1c6cc11891904b46ace0a7895d0d167d9bf5ce","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/commits/2e1c6cc11891904b46ace0a7895d0d167d9bf5ce"}],"sha":"fa54edfdd0e7a878f0d3dec25f869a895e19896b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/commits/fa54edfdd0e7a878f0d3dec25f869a895e19896b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3142325?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ddenysov","id":3142325,"login":"ddenysov","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxNDIzMjU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/commits/2e1c6cc11891904b46ace0a7895d0d167d9bf5ce/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-06-21T19:39:13Z","email":"denisov1985@gmail.com","name":"Dmytro Denysov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-06-21T19:39:13Z","email":"denisov1985@gmail.com","name":"Dmytro Denysov"},"message":"The changes implement Module Federation between a host and a remote application, both built with Vue 3 and Webpack. Here''s a breakdown of the changes and some suggestions:\n\n**Key Changes and Functionality**\n\n*   **Module Federation Setup:** Both `host` and `remote` now use Webpack''s `ModuleFederationPlugin`.\n    *   `remote` exposes its `App.vue` component as `remote/App`.  This allows the host to consume this component.\n    *   `host` declares `remote` as a remote application, specifying the URL to its `remoteEntry.js` (where the exposed modules are listed). It fetches the remote `App` component.\n*   **Remote Component Loading in Host:** `RemoteWrapper.vue` in `host` handles the dynamic import of the remote `App` component. It uses Vue''s `Suspense` to display a loading indicator while the remote component is being fetched and rendered.\n*   **Component Rendering:** The host''s `App.vue` now includes `<RemoteWrapper />`, which renders the remote application''s main component.\n*   **Port Change:** The remote application now runs on port 3000, while the host attempts to load the remote from port 3000 (originally 3001).\n*   **Styling Updates:** Minor styling adjustments in `remote/src/App.vue`.\n\n**Code Review and Suggestions**\n\n1.  **Port Consistency:** In `frontend/host/webpack.config.js`, the `remotes` configuration points to `http://localhost:3000/remoteEntry.js`.  Ensure that your remote application''s development server is indeed running on port 3000.  If it''s still on 3001, you''ll need to either change the port in the remote''s Webpack config or update this line in the host.\n\n2.  **Shared Dependencies (Removed):** The original `host/webpack.config.js` had a `shared` section for `vue`, enforcing a specific version.  This has been removed.  For production, it''s generally a good practice to share dependencies between host and remote applications to avoid loading the same library multiple times.  If both host and remote use Vue, consider re-adding a `shared` configuration like this to `host/webpack.config.js`:\n\n    ```javascript\n    shared: {\n      vue: {\n        singleton: true,\n        requiredVersion: \"^3.0.0\", // Or whatever version you''re using\n      },\n    },\n    ```\n\n    You will likely also want to share Vue in `remote/webpack.config.js`:\n\n    ```javascript\n    new ModuleFederationPlugin({\n      // ... other config\n      shared: {\n        vue: {\n          singleton: true,\n          requiredVersion: \"^3.0.0\", // Match the host''s version\n        },\n      },\n    }),\n    ```\n\n3.  **Error Handling:**  The `RemoteWrapper.vue` component uses `Suspense` for a loading state, but it lacks error handling.  If the remote component fails to load (e.g., network error, remote server down), the application will hang on the \"Загрузка...\" message.  Add an error state to provide a more user-friendly experience:\n\n    ```vue\n    <template>\n      <Suspense>\n        <component :is=\"remoteComponent\" />\n        <template #fallback>\n          <div>Загрузка...</div>\n        </template>\n      </Suspense>\n      <div v-if=\"error\" style=\"color: red;\">Ошибка загрузки компонента: {{ error }}</div>\n    </template>\n\n    <script setup>\n    import { ref } from ''vue'';\n\n    const remoteComponent = ref(null);\n    const error = ref(null); // Add an error ref\n\n    const load = async () => {\n      try {\n        const module = await import(\"remote/App\");\n        remoteComponent.value = module.default;\n      } catch (e) {\n        error.value = e.message || ''Unknown error''; // Capture the error\n      }\n    };\n\n    load();\n    </script>\n    ```\n\n4.  **Clarity in `webpack.config.js`:** In `remote/webpack.config.js` the `isRemoteDev` variable is declared but not used. This could be removed for better clarity.\n\n5.  **HTML Template Deduplication:** The HTML template in `remote/webpack.config.js` is almost identical to a standard Vue project''s `index.html`. Consider using a separate `index.html` file for the remote application instead of embedding it in `templateContent`.  This simplifies the Webpack configuration and makes it easier to manage the HTML.\n\n**To Test:**\n\n1.  Ensure both `host` and `remote` projects have their dependencies installed (`npm install`).\n2.  Start the development server for the `remote` application (e.g., `npm run serve` or the equivalent command defined in its `package.json`). Make sure it runs on port 3000.\n3.  Start the development server for the `host` application.\n4.  Access the host application in your browser. You should see content from both the host and the remote applications rendered together.\n\nBy addressing the suggestions above (port consistency, shared dependencies, error handling, and code clarity), you''ll have a more robust and maintainable Module Federation setup.","tree":{"sha":"800e6b77cb9958a3f75af3670bc65adab5fde6c3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/git/trees/800e6b77cb9958a3f75af3670bc65adab5fde6c3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/git/commits/2e1c6cc11891904b46ace0a7895d0d167d9bf5ce","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3142325?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ddenysov","id":3142325,"login":"ddenysov","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxNDIzMjU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ddenysov/canope/commit/2e1c6cc11891904b46ace0a7895d0d167d9bf5ce","node_id":"C_kwDOO2zci9oAKDJlMWM2Y2MxMTg5MTkwNGI0NmFjZTBhNzg5NWQwZDE2N2Q5YmY1Y2U","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ddenysov/canope/commit/6fb1f5bf155cc3f995828f2299b2105b7bfad2cd","sha":"6fb1f5bf155cc3f995828f2299b2105b7bfad2cd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/commits/6fb1f5bf155cc3f995828f2299b2105b7bfad2cd"}],"sha":"2e1c6cc11891904b46ace0a7895d0d167d9bf5ce","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/commits/2e1c6cc11891904b46ace0a7895d0d167d9bf5ce"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3142325?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ddenysov","id":3142325,"login":"ddenysov","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxNDIzMjU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/commits/6fb1f5bf155cc3f995828f2299b2105b7bfad2cd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-06-21T19:16:56Z","email":"denisov1985@gmail.com","name":"Dmytro Denysov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-06-21T19:16:56Z","email":"denisov1985@gmail.com","name":"Dmytro Denysov"},"message":"The changes implement Module Federation between a host and a remote application, both built with Vue 3 and Webpack. Here''s a breakdown of the changes and some suggestions:\n\n**Key Changes and Functionality**\n\n*   **Module Federation Setup:** Both `host` and `remote` now use Webpack''s `ModuleFederationPlugin`.\n    *   `remote` exposes its `App.vue` component as `remote/App`.  This allows the host to consume this component.\n    *   `host` declares `remote` as a remote application, specifying the URL to its `remoteEntry.js` (where the exposed modules are listed). It fetches the remote `App` component.\n*   **Remote Component Loading in Host:** `RemoteWrapper.vue` in `host` handles the dynamic import of the remote `App` component. It uses Vue''s `Suspense` to display a loading indicator while the remote component is being fetched and rendered.\n*   **Component Rendering:** The host''s `App.vue` now includes `<RemoteWrapper />`, which renders the remote application''s main component.\n*   **Port Change:** The remote application now runs on port 3000, while the host attempts to load the remote from port 3000 (originally 3001).\n*   **Styling Updates:** Minor styling adjustments in `remote/src/App.vue`.\n\n**Code Review and Suggestions**\n\n1.  **Port Consistency:** In `frontend/host/webpack.config.js`, the `remotes` configuration points to `http://localhost:3000/remoteEntry.js`.  Ensure that your remote application''s development server is indeed running on port 3000.  If it''s still on 3001, you''ll need to either change the port in the remote''s Webpack config or update this line in the host.\n\n2.  **Shared Dependencies (Removed):** The original `host/webpack.config.js` had a `shared` section for `vue`, enforcing a specific version.  This has been removed.  For production, it''s generally a good practice to share dependencies between host and remote applications to avoid loading the same library multiple times.  If both host and remote use Vue, consider re-adding a `shared` configuration like this to `host/webpack.config.js`:\n\n    ```javascript\n    shared: {\n      vue: {\n        singleton: true,\n        requiredVersion: \"^3.0.0\", // Or whatever version you''re using\n      },\n    },\n    ```\n\n    You will likely also want to share Vue in `remote/webpack.config.js`:\n\n    ```javascript\n    new ModuleFederationPlugin({\n      // ... other config\n      shared: {\n        vue: {\n          singleton: true,\n          requiredVersion: \"^3.0.0\", // Match the host''s version\n        },\n      },\n    }),\n    ```\n\n3.  **Error Handling:**  The `RemoteWrapper.vue` component uses `Suspense` for a loading state, but it lacks error handling.  If the remote component fails to load (e.g., network error, remote server down), the application will hang on the \"Загрузка...\" message.  Add an error state to provide a more user-friendly experience:\n\n    ```vue\n    <template>\n      <Suspense>\n        <component :is=\"remoteComponent\" />\n        <template #fallback>\n          <div>Загрузка...</div>\n        </template>\n      </Suspense>\n      <div v-if=\"error\" style=\"color: red;\">Ошибка загрузки компонента: {{ error }}</div>\n    </template>\n\n    <script setup>\n    import { ref } from ''vue'';\n\n    const remoteComponent = ref(null);\n    const error = ref(null); // Add an error ref\n\n    const load = async () => {\n      try {\n        const module = await import(\"remote/App\");\n        remoteComponent.value = module.default;\n      } catch (e) {\n        error.value = e.message || ''Unknown error''; // Capture the error\n      }\n    };\n\n    load();\n    </script>\n    ```\n\n4.  **Clarity in `webpack.config.js`:** In `remote/webpack.config.js` the `isRemoteDev` variable is declared but not used. This could be removed for better clarity.\n\n5.  **HTML Template Deduplication:** The HTML template in `remote/webpack.config.js` is almost identical to a standard Vue project''s `index.html`. Consider using a separate `index.html` file for the remote application instead of embedding it in `templateContent`.  This simplifies the Webpack configuration and makes it easier to manage the HTML.\n\n**To Test:**\n\n1.  Ensure both `host` and `remote` projects have their dependencies installed (`npm install`).\n2.  Start the development server for the `remote` application (e.g., `npm run serve` or the equivalent command defined in its `package.json`). Make sure it runs on port 3000.\n3.  Start the development server for the `host` application.\n4.  Access the host application in your browser. You should see content from both the host and the remote applications rendered together.\n\nBy addressing the suggestions above (port consistency, shared dependencies, error handling, and code clarity), you''ll have a more robust and maintainable Module Federation setup.","tree":{"sha":"6f4b7872536f91f2d8270bd813b07abae2f0996c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/git/trees/6f4b7872536f91f2d8270bd813b07abae2f0996c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/git/commits/6fb1f5bf155cc3f995828f2299b2105b7bfad2cd","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3142325?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ddenysov","id":3142325,"login":"ddenysov","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxN