** A new target `create-static-volume` has been added to create a Docker volume named `static-data`.\n*   **frontend/root/docker-compose.yml & frontend/sign-up/docker-compose.yml:** Both files now include:\n    *   A shared volume `static-data` mounted to `/static`.\n    *   The `static-data` volume is defined as external, meaning it should already exist.\n\n**Suggestions:**\n\n1.  **Dependencies for `sign-up` Frontend:** The removal of `yarn.lock` and potentially `package.json` (not provided) means the `sign-up` frontend may not have explicitly defined dependencies anymore. If it relies on shared dependencies, ensure they are correctly managed in the root project or another shared configuration. Otherwise, consider generating `package.json` and `yarn.lock` with explicitly defined dependencies.\n2.  **Consistency in Dependency Management:** Confirm that the project consistently uses either `npm` or `yarn` for dependency management. Mixing them can lead to issues.\n3.  **`publicPath` Configuration:** In `frontend/sign-up/vue.config.js` confirm if it is needed.\n4.  **Environment Variables**: Review to confirm if the environment variable `NODE_ENV=development` is useful or needed.","tree":{"sha":"8bbad79b7744fb09b4dc690f71443d3e96d3160f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/git/trees/8bbad79b7744fb09b4dc690f71443d3e96d3160f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/git/commits/fcb160ad3ecc801501a7cbe1ec66e0718e1f5ce7","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3142325?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ddenysov","id":3142325,"login":"ddenysov","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxNDIzMjU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ddenysov/canope/commit/fcb160ad3ecc801501a7cbe1ec66e0718e1f5ce7","node_id":"C_kwDOO2zci9oAKGZjYjE2MGFkM2VjYzgwMTUwMWE3Y2JlMWVjNjZlMDcxOGUxZjVjZTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ddenysov/canope/commit/eb36b69a63b929a10fbc1ec431ff3f24a88b230d","sha":"eb36b69a63b929a10fbc1ec431ff3f24a88b230d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/commits/eb36b69a63b929a10fbc1ec431ff3f24a88b230d"}],"sha":"fcb160ad3ecc801501a7cbe1ec66e0718e1f5ce7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/commits/fcb160ad3ecc801501a7cbe1ec66e0718e1f5ce7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3142325?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ddenysov","id":3142325,"login":"ddenysov","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxNDIzMjU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/commits/eb36b69a63b929a10fbc1ec431ff3f24a88b230d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-06-16T19:56:24Z","email":"denisov1985@gmail.com","name":"Dmytro Denysov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-06-16T19:56:24Z","email":"denisov1985@gmail.com","name":"Dmytro Denysov"},"message":"The provided diffs introduce new configuration files for Nginx and Docker Compose, setting up a development environment for two frontend applications: `root-config` and `hello-world`.  Let''s break down the changes and offer some observations:\n\n**Key Changes and Observations**\n\n*   **New Configuration Files:**  The core change is the addition of three new files: `sign-up-config.conf`, `root-config.conf`, and `docker-compose.yml`. These files work together to define the Nginx server configurations and the Docker Compose setup for the frontend applications.  Note: The file `sign-up-config.conf` is present but not used in the `docker-compose.yml` file, so it''s likely for a separate part of the system not reflected in these diffs.\n\n*   **Nginx Configurations:**  `root-config.conf` and (presumably) `sign-up-config.conf` (though not directly included in the Compose setup here) define Nginx server blocks.  They both:\n    *   Listen on port 80.\n    *   Serve static files from `/usr/share/nginx/html`.\n    *   Use `index.html` as the default file.\n    *   Use `try_files $uri $uri/ /index.html;` for routing, enabling single-page application (SPA) routing.\n    *   Enable CORS for various file types (`js`, `css`, `json`, `wasm`). The `root-config.conf` additionally enables CORS for `/import-map.json`, which suggests the application may use SystemJS or a similar module loader with import maps.\n\n*   **Docker Compose Setup:** The `docker-compose.yml` file defines two services:\n    *   `root-config`:  Runs an Nginx container for the `root-config` application, mapping port 9000 on the host to port 80 in the container.  It mounts the application''s `dist` directory and the Nginx configuration file.\n    *   `hello-world`:  Similarly, sets up an Nginx container for the `hello-world` application, mapping port 8500 to port 80 and mounting the corresponding files.\n\n**Possible Improvements**\n\n*   **CORS Security:** While `Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *` allows requests from any origin, it''s not ideal for production.  Consider restricting this to specific domains or using a more sophisticated CORS configuration when deploying.\n\n*   **Configuration File Organization:**  The diff shows Nginx configurations stored directly in the `frontend/static` directory.  It might be clearer to group them into a dedicated `nginx` subdirectory within `frontend/static`.  The `docker-compose.yml` reflects this suggested structure, referencing  `./nginx/root-config.conf` and `./nginx/hello-world.conf`.\n\n*   **Missing `sign-up-config` Integration:** The `sign-up-config.conf` isn''t used in the provided Docker Compose configuration. If it''s meant to be part of this setup, it should be added as a service with its own port and volume mappings.\n\n*   **Shared Nginx Base Configuration:** The `root-config.conf` and `hello-world.conf` (not shown, but implied by `docker-compose.yml`) likely share similar settings. For maintainability, consider using a base or shared configuration file and including or extending it in the specific service configurations.  This reduces duplication.\n\n**Example of a Possible Improvement (Shared Config)**\n\nTo illustrate the shared configuration point, you could restructure the `nginx` directory like this:\n\n```\nfrontend/static/nginx/\n├── base.conf  # Shared settings\n├── root-config.conf  # Specific to root-config\n└── hello-world.conf # Specific to hello-world\n```\n\nThen, in `root-config.conf`, you might have:\n\n```nginx\ninclude /etc/nginx/conf.d/base.conf;\n\nserver {\n  # ... specific root-config settings ...\n}\n```\n\nAnd similarly in `hello-world.conf`.  The `base.conf` would contain the common parts like CORS, root directory, index file, etc.  You''d adjust the volume mapping in `docker-compose.yml` to reflect this change:\n\n```yaml\n      - ./nginx/root-config.conf:/etc/nginx/conf.d/default.conf:ro\n```\n\n**Conclusion**\n\nThe provided configuration establishes a basic development environment for two frontend applications using Nginx and Docker Compose. The suggested improvements aim to enhance organization, maintainability, and security. Remember to address the CORS wildcard before deploying to a production environment.","tree":{"sha":"63d9a1356b73beedfaf713301c8bab5ef1ff19ae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/git/trees/63d9a1356b73beedfaf713301c8bab5ef1ff19ae"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/git/commits/eb36b69a63b929a10fbc1ec431ff3f24a88b230d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3142325?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ddenysov","id":3142325,"login":"ddenysov","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxNDIzMjU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ddenysov/canope/commit/eb36b69a63b929a10fbc1ec431ff3f24a88b230d","node_id":"C_kwDOO2zci9oAKGViMzZiNjlhNjNiOTI5YTEwZmJjMWVjNDMxZmYzZjI0YTg4YjIzMGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ddenysov/canope/commit/a27204dcd8e585d2899375e23192f5c872c538a3","sha":"a27204dcd8e585d2899375e23192f5c872c538a3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/commits/a27204dcd8e585d2899375e23192f5c872c538a3"}],"sha":"eb36b69a63b929a10fbc1ec431ff3f24a88b230d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/commits/eb36b69a63b929a10fbc1ec431ff3f24a88b230d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3142325?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ddenysov","id":3142325,"login":"ddenysov","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxNDIzMjU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/commits/a27204dcd8e585d2899375e23192f5c872c538a3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-06-16T19:48:04Z","email":"denisov1985@gmail.com","name":"Dmytro Denysov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-06-16T19:48:04Z","email":"denisov1985@gmail.com","name":"Dmytro Denysov"},"message":"Okay, I will review the provided files and identify areas for improvement.\n\n**frontend/root/yarn.lock**\n\nThis file has been deleted. As a general practice, it''s good to keep your dependencies up to date and remove unused ones.\n\n**infra/docker/node/v24/Dockerfile**\n\nThe Dockerfile looks good, and here are some possible improvements:\n\n*   Specify a non-root user:  To enhance security, create a non-root user and assign ownership of the `/app` directory to that user.\n*   Use multi-stage builds: This involves using one stage to build the application and another to run it, resulting in a smaller final image.\n\n```dockerfile\nFROM node:24 AS builder\n\nWORKDIR /app\n\nCOPY package*.json ./\nRUN npm install\n\nCOPY . .\n\nRUN npm run build\n\nFROM node:24-slim\nWORKDIR /app\n\nCOPY --from=builder /app/dist ./dist\nCOPY --from=builder /app/package*.json ./\n\nRUN npm install --production\n\nEXPOSE 9000\n\nCMD [\"node\", \"dist/index.js\"]\n```\n\n**frontend/root/docker-compose.yml**\n\nThe docker-compose.yml file is well constructed.\n\nOverall, the provided configuration is pretty standard and simple, but could benefit from the suggested improvements.","tree":{"sha":"1ab16e7a94cf4805986a52f0380e11f3793fbce8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/git/trees/1ab16e7a94cf4805986a52f0380e11f3793fbce8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/git/commits/a27204dcd8e585d2899375e23192f5c872c538a3","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3142325?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ddenysov","id":3142325,"login":"ddenysov","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxNDIzMjU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/rec