:false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/commits/64bfe5647d144b7893ab7490da9333b885589efd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-06-14T19:17:14Z","email":"denisov1985@gmail.com","name":"Dmytro Denysov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-06-14T19:17:14Z","email":"denisov1985@gmail.com","name":"Dmytro Denysov"},"message":"Okay, I''ve reviewed the changes and here are my observations and suggestions:\n\n**General Observations:**\n\n*   The changes introduce a basic single-spa setup with a root config and a sample Vue.js microfrontend.\n*   The configuration uses import maps for managing dependencies, which is a good practice for single-spa applications.\n*   The code includes necessary webpack configurations, eslint configurations, and package.json files for both the root config and the microfrontend.\n\n**Specific Suggestions and Improvements:**\n\n*   **Root Config - `src/index.ejs`:** The `index.ejs` file is well-structured. However, consider externalizing the import map into a separate JSON file (e.g., `importmap.json`) for easier management, especially in production environments.\n*   **Root Config - `src/canope-root-config.ts`:** The root config file is straightforward and uses `single-spa-layout` effectively.\n*   **Microfrontend Layout - `src/microfrontend-layout.html`:** This file defines the layout for the microfrontends, which is a core part of `single-spa-layout`. It uses `<single-spa-router>` and `<route>` elements to define how microfrontends are displayed based on the URL.\n*   **Sign-up Microfrontend - `src/main.js`:** This file correctly exports the `bootstrap`, `mount`, and `unmount` lifecycle functions, which are required for a single-spa application.\n\nOverall, the code provides a solid foundation for a single-spa application. The suggestions above mainly focus on improving maintainability and scalability.","tree":{"sha":"c0311ca7d93a2a82cddfa3f7182b157be5015b06","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/git/trees/c0311ca7d93a2a82cddfa3f7182b157be5015b06"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/git/commits/64bfe5647d144b7893ab7490da9333b885589efd","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3142325?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ddenysov","id":3142325,"login":"ddenysov","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxNDIzMjU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ddenysov/canope/commit/64bfe5647d144b7893ab7490da9333b885589efd","node_id":"C_kwDOO2zci9oAKDY0YmZlNTY0N2QxNDRiNzg5M2FiNzQ5MGRhOTMzM2I4ODU1ODllZmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ddenysov/canope/commit/4f748b33920557d3dcfa70346f1086d7ac9cb755","sha":"4f748b33920557d3dcfa70346f1086d7ac9cb755","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/commits/4f748b33920557d3dcfa70346f1086d7ac9cb755"}],"sha":"64bfe5647d144b7893ab7490da9333b885589efd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/commits/64bfe5647d144b7893ab7490da9333b885589efd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3142325?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ddenysov","id":3142325,"login":"ddenysov","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxNDIzMjU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/commits/4f748b33920557d3dcfa70346f1086d7ac9cb755/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-06-13T13:34:04Z","email":"denisov1985@gmail.com","name":"Dmytro Denysov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-06-13T13:34:04Z","email":"denisov1985@gmail.com","name":"Dmytro Denysov"},"message":"This code introduces several improvements and new features, primarily focused on enhancing API responses and data handling. Here''s a breakdown:\n\n**Key Changes and Improvements:**\n\n*   **Simplified Response Handling:** The code replaces custom collection responses (`PingCollection`, `PingCollectionResponse`) with a more generic `ResourceCollection` within the core library.  This promotes reusability and reduces redundancy.  The `ListController` now directly returns a `JsonResponse` containing a `PingResource::collection` which leverages this new mechanism.\n\n*   **Resource Collections:** A new `ResourceCollection` class is introduced in `libs/core/src/Http/Resource/ResourceCollection.php`.  This class handles the formatting of collections of resources for API responses, including pagination and links. It implements `JsonSerializable` for easy conversion to JSON.\n\n*   **URL Generation:** The `Url` class in `libs/core/src/Support/Url/Url.php` gains a `path()` method. This method constructs URLs based on the current request URI and provided query parameters, crucial for generating pagination links within resource collections.\n\n*   **Pagination Enhancements:**\n    *   The `PingListQueryHandler` now correctly calculates the offset for pagination using `$query->getOffset()` and passes it to the `QueryOptions` used in the data store query.\n    *   It also fetches the total count of items using  `$this->store->count(''read_model_users'')` to accurately populate pagination metadata.\n    *   The `ListQuery` class gets a `getOffset()` method to calculate the offset based on page size and number.\n    *   The `PdoDataStore` class in `libs/core/src/DataStore/Bridge/PDO/PdoDataStore.php` implements the `count()` method using a `COUNT(*)` query.\n\n*   **Resource Linking:**  The `PingResource` class now includes a `getUrl()` method, which returns the base URL for individual resource links.\n\n*   **JSON API Compliance:**  The changes aim to produce responses that are more compliant with the JSON:API specification, particularly in how collections and pagination are represented.\n\n**Code Style and Consistency:**\n\n*   The code maintains good practices like strict typing (`declare(strict_types=1);`) and consistent use of namespaces.\n\n**Suggestions and Potential Improvements:**\n\n*   **Error Handling:**  The code doesn''t explicitly show error handling.  Consider adding mechanisms to handle potential exceptions (e.g., database errors) and return appropriate error responses.\n\n*   **Type Hinting:** While generally good, ensure all methods and function parameters have consistent and accurate type hinting for better code clarity and maintainability.\n\n*   **Configuration:**  The base URL for links (e.g., in `PingResource::getUrl()`) might be hardcoded.  Consider using a configuration system to manage such values.\n\n*   **Testing:**  It''s crucial to have unit and integration tests to verify the correctness of these changes, especially the pagination and URL generation logic.\n\n**Overall:**\n\nThe changes represent a significant step towards a more robust and standardized API.  The introduction of `ResourceCollection` and the improved pagination handling are particularly valuable.  Remember to address the suggestions above to further enhance the code''s quality and reliability.","tree":{"sha":"2d3ecbedde4c5e2d68c7d3c9da4014093f46f68a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/git/trees/2d3ecbedde4c5e2d68c7d3c9da4014093f46f68a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/git/commits/4f748b33920557d3dcfa70346f1086d7ac9cb755","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3142325?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ddenysov","id":3142325,"login":"ddenysov","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxNDIzMjU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ddenysov/canope/commit/4f748b33920557d3dcfa70346f1086d7ac9cb755","node_id":"C_kwDOO2zci9oAKDRmNzQ4YjMzOTIwNTU3ZDNkY2ZhNzAzNDZmMTA4NmQ3YWM5Y2I3NTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ddenysov/canope/commit/c1ddf7a4091755abb286b39651dfcee27848b743","sha":"c1ddf7a4091755abb286b39651dfcee27848b743","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/commits/c1ddf7a4091755abb286b39651dfcee27848b743"}],"sha":"4f748b33920557d3dcfa70346f1086d7ac9cb755","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/commits/4f748b33920557d3dcfa70346f1086d7ac9cb755"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3142325?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ddenysov","id":3142325,"login":"ddenysov","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxNDIzMjU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/commits/c1ddf7a4091755abb286b39651dfcee27848b743/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-06-13T10:13:51Z","email":"denisov1985@gmail.com","name":"Dmytro Denysov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-06-13T10:13:51Z","email":"denisov1985@gmail.com","name":"Dmytro Denysov"},"message":"The following changes have been made:\n\n*   Added environment variable support to the `docker-compose.yml` file for the user service.\n*   Removed the unused `$id` property from the `FindPingQuery` class.\n*   Modified the `IndexController` to inject the command bus via the constructor and use it within the `__invoke` method. Also removed the logger as it was not being used.\n*   Added application URL and development configuration to the `.env` file.\n*   Simplified the `ViewController` by directly passing the ID in the `FindPingQuery` constructor and streamlining the response creation.\n*   Refactored the `PingResource` to extend `AbstractResource`, implementing the required methods for JSON serialization and type definition.\n*   Added a new `Url` class in the `core` library to handle URL generation based on environment variables or request parameters.\n*   Updated `JsonApiCollectionResponse` to use the new `Url` class for generating pagination links.\n*   Introduced `AbstractResource` in the `core` library as a base class for resources, providing common functionality for JSON serialization and attribute mapping.","tree":{"sha":"b62806e994fc7da52fae9c080a7e40a2b09c3a77","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/git/trees/b62806e994fc7da52fae9c080a7e40a2b09c3a77"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/git/commits/c1ddf7a4091755abb286b39651dfcee27848b743","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3142325?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ddenysov","id":3142325,"login":"ddenysov","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxNDIzMjU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ddenysov/canope/commit/c1ddf7a4091755abb286b39651dfcee27848b743","node_id":"C_kwDOO2zci9oAKGMxZGRmN2E0MDkxNzU1YWJiMjg2YjM5NjUxZGZjZWUyNzg0OGI3NDM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ddenysov/canope/commit/bb30fc22ea8ae86171f508020072a1c190f45e90","sha":"bb30fc22ea8ae86171f508020072a1c190f45e90","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/commits/bb30fc22ea8ae86171f508020072a1c190f45e90"}],"sha":"c1ddf7a4091755abb286b39651dfcee27848b743","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/commits/c1ddf7a4091755abb286b39651dfcee27848b743"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3142325?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ddenysov","id":3142325,"login":"ddenysov","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxNDIzMjU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/commits/bb30fc22ea8ae86171f508020072a1c190f45e90/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-06-12T19:54:30Z","email":"denisov1985@gmail.com","name":"Dmytro Denysov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-06-12T19:54:30Z","email":"denisov1985@gmail.com","name":"Dmytro Denysov"},"message":"The code changes look good! Here''s a breakdown of the improvements:\n\n*   **RESTful API:** The route for viewing a user is updated to include an ID parameter (`/view/{id}`), aligning with REST principles.\n*   **Resource Classes:** The introduction of `PingResource` helps encapsulate the data transformation logic for a single \"ping\" object, making the controller leaner and the response structure consistent.\n*   **Collection Handling:** The `PingCollection` class (formerly `PingCollectionResponse`) now utilizes `PingResource` for each item in the collection, further standardizing the output format.  The base class `JsonApiCollectionResponse` is also updated to use a resource class, reducing redundancy.\n*   **Query Handling:** The `ViewController` now directly receives the ID, simplifying the request handling within the controller.\n*   **Data Retrieval:** The `PingListQueryHandler` now correctly uses `QueryOptions` to pass the page size to the data store.\n\nThere are no immediate code suggestions for this diff. The changes seem well-organized and improve the structure and maintainability of the API responses.","tree":{"sha":"de058fe49c73a6066617f18a1f20f3292b7d6b02","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/git/trees/de058fe49c73a6066617f18a1f20f3292b7d6b02"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/git/commits/bb30fc22ea8ae86171f508020072a1c190f45e90","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3142325?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ddenysov","id":3142325,"login":"ddenysov","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxNDIzMjU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ddenysov","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ddenysov/canope/commit/bb30fc22ea8ae86171f508020072a1c190f45e90","node_id":"C_kwDOO2zci9oAKGJiMzBmYzIyZWE4YWU4NjE3MWY1MDgwMjAwNzJhMWMxOTBmNDVlOTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ddenysov/canope/commit/1edc1ae309848bf674cbb1a152060c9bc6b390e6","sha":"1edc1ae309848bf674cbb1a152060c9bc6b390e6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/commits/1edc1ae309848bf674cbb1a152060c9bc6b390e6"}],"sha":"bb30fc22ea8ae86171f508020072a1c190f45e90","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/commits/bb30fc22ea8ae86171f508020072a1c190f45e90"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/commits/1edc1ae309848bf674cbb1a152060c9bc6b390e6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-06-12T19:49:37Z","email":"dmytro.denysov@danads.se","name":"Dmytro Denysov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-06-12T19:49:37Z","email":"dmytro.denysov@danads.se","name":"Dmytro Denysov"},"message":"The code changes look good! Here''s a breakdown of the improvements:\n\n*   **RESTful API:** The route for viewing a user is updated to include an ID parameter (`/view/{id}`), aligning with REST principles.\n*   **Resource Classes:** The introduction of `PingResource` helps encapsulate the data transformation logic for a single \"ping\" object, making the controller leaner and the response structure consistent.\n*   **Collection Handling:** The `PingCollection` class (formerly `PingCollectionResponse`) now utilizes `PingResource` for each item in the collection, further standardizing the output format.  The base class `JsonApiCollectionResponse` is also updated to use a resource class, reducing redundancy.\n*   **Query Handling:** The `ViewController` now directly receives the ID, simplifying the request handling within the controller.\n*   **Data Retrieval:** The `PingListQueryHandler` now correctly uses `QueryOptions` to pass the page size to the data store.\n\nThere are no immediate code suggestions for this diff. The changes seem well-organized and improve the structure and maintainability of the API responses.","tree":{"sha":"21cd3fd0af4ec198beb42abaed7c39ecbb444511","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/git/trees/21cd3fd0af4ec198beb42abaed7c39ecbb444511"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/git/commits/1edc1ae309848bf674cbb1a152060c9bc6b390e6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/ddenysov/canope/commit/1edc1ae309848bf674cbb1a152060c9bc6b390e6","node_id":"C_kwDOO2zci9oAKDFlZGMxYWUzMDk4NDhiZjY3NGNiYjFhMTUyMDYwYzliYzZiMzkwZTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ddenysov/canope/commit/8f10c0e7e560069cb718d51943e6b9c6ceb7506a","sha":"8f10c0e7e560069cb718d51943e6b9c6ceb7506a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/commits/8f10c0e7e560069cb718d51943e6b9c6ceb7506a"}],"sha":"1edc1ae309848bf674cbb1a152060c9bc6b390e6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/commits/1edc1ae309848bf674cbb1a152060c9bc6b390e6"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/commits/8f10c0e7e560069cb718d51943e6b9c6ceb7506a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-06-12T15:24:06Z","email":"dmytro.denysov@danads.se","name":"Dmytro Denysov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-06-12T15:24:06Z","email":"dmytro.denysov@danads.se","name":"Dmytro Denysov"},"message":"The following changes were made:\n* Moved the controller classes into a sub-directory named `Controller` and updated the namespaces accordingly.\n* Updated the `services.yaml` and `routes.yaml` files to reflect the new controller locations.\n* Created a new `PingCollectionResponse` class to encapsulate the JSON API response for a collection of \"pings\", including mapping attributes and defining the resource type.\n* Modified the base `JsonApiCollectionResponse` class to be abstract, and delegated the responsibility of mapping attributes and defining the resource type to concrete subclasses.","tree":{"sha":"28137d55e1bc62fe388ecf2b0d2abf2f720859f1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/git/trees/28137d55e1bc62fe388ecf2b0d2abf2f720859f1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/git/commits/8f10c0e7e560069cb718d51943e6b9c6ceb7506a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/ddenysov/canope/commit/8f10c0e7e560069cb718d51943e6b9c6ceb7506a","node_id":"C_kwDOO2zci9oAKDhmMTBjMGU3ZTU2MDA2OWNiNzE4ZDUxOTQzZTZiOWM2Y2ViNzUwNmE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ddenysov/canope/commit/0d3cf29ca88113aa29e42f769054ef8626a2c905","sha":"0d3cf29ca88113aa29e42f769054ef8626a2c905","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/commits/0d3cf29ca88113aa29e42f769054ef8626a2c905"}],"sha":"8f10c0e7e560069cb718d51943e6b9c6ceb7506a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/commits/8f10c0e7e560069cb718d51943e6b9c6ceb7506a"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/commits/0d3cf29ca88113aa29e42f769054ef8626a2c905/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-06-12T15:04:09Z","email":"dmytro.denysov@danads.se","name":"Dmytro Denysov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-06-12T15:04:09Z","email":"dmytro.denysov@danads.se","name":"Dmytro Denysov"},"message":"The code changes introduce a new query system for handling list requests in a user service, leveraging interfaces and classes for better structure and functionality. Here''s a breakdown:\n\n**Key Changes:**\n\n*   **`QueryBusInterface.php`:** The return type of the `dispatch` method is changed from `array` to `mixed`, allowing for more flexible query results.\n*   **`PaginatedResult.php`:**  Simplifies the `PaginatedResult` class by removing the `JsonSerializable` interface and some pagination details (page, perPage), keeping only items and total count. This suggests pagination logic might be handled elsewhere, likely in the response formatting.\n*   **`ListController.php`:** This controller now uses a `QueryBusInterface` to dispatch a `PingListQuery` and returns a `JsonApiCollectionResponse`. It also uses `MapQueryString` to map query parameters to the `PingListQuery`.\n*   **`MessengerQueryBus.php`:**  The `dispatch` method now returns `mixed`, aligning with the interface change. It also removes the check that the result is an array, further supporting flexible return types.\n*   **`ListQueryHandlerInterface.php`:** Defines an interface for handling `ListQuery` types, ensuring a consistent structure for list query handlers.\n*   **`PingListQueryHandler.php`:**  This class handles the `PingListQuery`, retrieving data from a `DataStoreInterface` and returning a `PaginatedResult`. Note that the total count is currently hardcoded to 123.\n*   **`JsonApiCollectionResponse.php`:** This class formats the paginated result into a JSON API compliant response, including data, metadata (pagination details), and links for navigation.  It constructs links for `self`, `first`, `prev`, `next`, and `last` pages based on the query parameters and a hardcoded base URL and total pages (100). The total count in meta is hardcoded to 123.\n*   **`ListQuery.php`:** This class now implements `QueryInterface` and includes a `toArray` method (currently a stub).\n*   **`PingListQuery.php`:** A specific implementation of `ListQuery` for the user service.\n\n**Improvements and Considerations:**\n\n*   **Hardcoded Values:** The total count in `PingListQueryHandler` and pagination details (total, totalPages) in `JsonApiCollectionResponse` are hardcoded.  These should be dynamically calculated based on the actual data and pagination settings.\n*   **Base URL:** The base URL for constructing links in `JsonApiCollectionResponse` is hardcoded. This should be configurable, possibly through environment variables or a configuration service.\n*   **`toArray` Method:** The `toArray` method in `ListQuery` is not implemented. Consider if this method is needed and implement it accordingly.\n*   **Error Handling:** The code lacks explicit error handling for scenarios like query dispatch failures or data store errors.\n*   **Testing:**  Consider adding unit and integration tests for the new query system components.\n\n**Code Suggestions:**\n\n1.  **Dynamic Pagination:**\n    *   In `PingListQueryHandler`, retrieve the total count from the `DataStoreInterface` instead of hardcoding it:\n\n    ```php\n    public function __invoke(PingListQuery $query): PaginatedResult\n    {\n        $items = $this->store->find(\n            ''read_model_users'',\n        );\n        $total = $this->store->count(''read_model_users''); // Assuming a count method exists\n\n        return new PaginatedResult($items, $total);\n    }\n    ```\n\n    *   In `JsonApiCollectionResponse`, calculate `totalPages` and use the actual `$result->total`:\n\n    ```php\n    $totalPages = (int) ceil($result->total / $query->pageSize);\n    // ...\n    ''meta''  => [\n        ''page'' => [\n            ''number''     => $query->pageNumber,\n            ''size''       => $query->pageSize,\n            ''total''      => $result->total,\n            ''totalPages'' => $totalPages,\n        ],\n    ],\n    ```\n\n2.  **Configurable Base URL:** Inject the base URL into `JsonApiCollectionResponse` (e.g., via constructor injection) or retrieve it from a configuration service.\n\n3.  **Implement `toArray`:** If `toArray` is needed in `ListQuery`, implement it to return an array representation of the query (e.g., for serialization or caching).\n\n4.  **Consider returning an empty array instead of null for prev and next links:**\n\n    ```php\n    ''links'' => [\n        ''self''  => $buildLink($query->pageNumber),\n        ''first'' => $buildLink(1),\n        ''prev''  => $query->pageNumber > 1 ? $buildLink($query->pageNumber - 1) : [],\n        ''next''  => $query->pageNumber < $totalPages ? $buildLink($query->pageNumber + 1) : [],\n        ''last''  => $buildLink($totalPages),\n    ],\n    ```\n\nThese changes improve the accuracy and flexibility of the pagination and response generation.","tree":{"sha":"65f975d06fd638008377a15d2d3475afb17e9986","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/git/trees/65f975d06fd638008377a15d2d3475afb17e9986"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/git/commits/0d3cf29ca88113aa29e42f769054ef8626a2c905","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/ddenysov/canope/commit/0d3cf29ca88113aa29e42f769054ef8626a2c905","node_id":"C_kwDOO2zci9oAKDBkM2NmMjljYTg4MTEzYWEyOWU0MmY3NjkwNTRlZjg2MjZhMmM5MDU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ddenysov/canope/commit/6c7d5d624cf2e0139f3bf01208b0cfea046189aa","sha":"6c7d5d624cf2e0139f3bf01208b0cfea046189aa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/commits/6c7d5d624cf2e0139f3bf01208b0cfea046189aa"}],"sha":"0d3cf29ca88113aa29e42f769054ef8626a2c905","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/commits/0d3cf29ca88113aa29e42f769054ef8626a2c905"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/commits/6c7d5d624cf2e0139f3bf01208b0cfea046189aa/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-06-12T13:36:28Z","email":"dmytro.denysov@danads.se","name":"Dmytro Denysov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-06-12T13:36:28Z","email":"dmytro.denysov@danads.se","name":"Dmytro Denysov"},"message":"I will review the code and provide feedback.\n\nThe changes introduce a system for handling list queries in a Symfony application, specifically designed to integrate with JSON:API standards. Here''s a breakdown:\n\n**Key Components:**\n\n*   **`JsonApiListQueryFactoryInterface`**: An interface defining a factory method for creating list queries from an array, adhering to JSON:API structure.\n*   **`ListQuery`**: A class representing a list query with properties for pagination, sorting, filtering, and searching. It implements `JsonApiListQueryFactoryInterface` to enable creation from JSON:API-style arrays.\n*   **`MapQueryString`**: An attribute used to mark controller parameters that should be populated from the query string.\n*   **`MapQueryStringResolver`**: A value resolver that handles the logic of mapping query string parameters to the corresponding `ListQuery` object (or other classes implementing `JsonApiListQueryFactoryInterface`). It supports both direct property mapping and JSON:API array-based creation.\n*   **`ListController`**: An example controller demonstrating how to use the `MapQueryString` attribute to receive a `ListQuery` object populated from the request''s query string.\n\n**Improvements and Suggestions:**\n\n1.  **Error Handling**: In `MapQueryStringResolver`, the code throws an `InvalidArgumentException` if the target class doesn''t exist. Consider adding more specific error handling or logging for cases where query parameters cannot be mapped to properties (e.g., due to type mismatch or non-public properties).\n\n2.  **JSON:API Compliance**:  The `ListQuery::fromJsonApiArray` method currently only handles `page[number]` and `page[size]`. To be fully compliant with JSON:API, it should also handle `sort` and `filter`.\n\n    ```php\n    #[\\Override] public static function fromJsonApiArray(array $array): static\n    {\n        $instance = new self();\n        $instance->pageNumber = isset($array[''page''][''number'']) ? (int)$array[''page''][''number''] : 1;\n        $instance->pageSize = isset($array[''page''][''size'']) ? (int)$array[''page''][''size''] : 25; // Use default from property\n\n        if (isset($array[''sort''])) {\n            $instance->sort = $array[''sort''];\n        }\n\n        if (isset($array[''filter''])) {\n            $instance->filter = $array[''filter''];\n            if (isset($array[''filter''][''search''])) {\n                $instance->search = $array[''filter''][''search''];\n                unset($instance->filter[''search'']); // Remove search from general filters\n            }\n        }\n\n        return $instance;\n    }\n    ```\n\n3.  **Default Page Size**: In `ListQuery::fromJsonApiArray`, the default page size is hardcoded to `10`. It should be consistent with the default value of the `$pageSize` property (which is `25`).  I''ve corrected this in the suggestion above.\n\n4.  **Type Handling in Resolver**: The `MapQueryStringResolver` uses `settype` for type coercion.  While functional, this can lead to unexpected behavior. A more robust approach would be to use a dedicated type conversion library or implement custom conversion logic with validation.  For example, you might want to throw an exception if a string value cannot be safely converted to an integer for `pageNumber` or `pageSize`.\n\n5.  **Sort String Format**: The comment for the `$sort` property in `ListQuery` mentions a comma-separated string format (e.g., `sort=-created_at,name`).  Consider adding logic to parse this string into an array or a more structured format for easier use within the application.\n\n6.  **List Controller**: The `ListController` is a good example, but it currently only returns pagination information. Expand it to demonstrate how to use the other properties of the `ListQuery` object (sorting, filtering, etc.) to retrieve and return data.\n\n7.  **Testing**:  Add unit tests for the `MapQueryStringResolver` and `ListQuery` to ensure they handle various query string scenarios and JSON:API structures correctly. Include tests for error cases (invalid types, missing parameters, etc.).\n\n**Overall:**\n\nThis is a well-structured implementation for handling list queries with JSON:API support in a Symfony application. The suggestions above aim to improve its robustness, compliance, and usability.  Remember to adapt the code to fit the specific requirements and data structures of your project.","tree":{"sha":"0a6932bccf8d657a9d9bc79312cf636d8694f936","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/git/trees/0a6932bccf8d657a9d9bc79312cf636d8694f936"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/git/commits/6c7d5d624cf2e0139f3bf01208b0cfea046189aa","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/ddenysov/canope/commit/6c7d5d624cf2e0139f3bf01208b0cfea046189aa","node_id":"C_kwDOO2zci9oAKDZjN2Q1ZDYyNGNmMmUwMTM5ZjNiZjAxMjA4YjBjZmVhMDQ2MTg5YWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ddenysov/canope/commit/1109ae1a9923936b00af74b9ef5df8e54a883f3f","sha":"1109ae1a9923936b00af74b9ef5df8e54a883f3f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/commits/1109ae1a9923936b00af74b9ef5df8e54a883f3f"}],"sha":"6c7d5d624cf2e0139f3bf01208b0cfea046189aa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/commits/6c7d5d624cf2e0139f3bf01208b0cfea046189aa"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/commits/1109ae1a9923936b00af74b9ef5df8e54a883f3f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-06-10T19:17:03Z","email":"dmytro.denysov@danads.se","name":"Dmytro Denysov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-06-10T19:17:03Z","email":"dmytro.denysov@danads.se","name":"Dmytro Denysov"},"message":"It looks like you''re renaming `CollectionQuery.php` to `ListQuery.php` and updating the class name within the file to reflect this change.  This seems like a straightforward refactoring step to better reflect the purpose of the class. Is there anything specific you''d like me to check or any further actions related to this change?","tree":{"sha":"b890c3738a5f51b006aeddd4c3da4b01c4b60cf4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/git/trees/b890c3738a5f51b006aeddd4c3da4b01c4b60cf4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/git/commits/1109ae1a9923936b00af74b9ef5df8e54a883f3f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/ddenysov/canope/commit/1109ae1a9923936b00af74b9ef5df8e54a883f3f","node_id":"C_kwDOO2zci9oAKDExMDlhZTFhOTkyMzkzNmIwMGFmNzRiOWVmNWRmOGU1NGE4ODNmM2Y","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ddenysov/canope/commit/5bc9c0218170c59e1e2500511b9fbfc59cbd9694","sha":"5bc9c0218170c59e1e2500511b9fbfc59cbd9694","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/commits/5bc9c0218170c59e1e2500511b9fbfc59cbd9694"}],"sha":"1109ae1a9923936b00af74b9ef5df8e54a883f3f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/commits/1109ae1a9923936b00af74b9ef5df8e54a883f3f"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/commits/5bc9c0218170c59e1e2500511b9fbfc59cbd9694/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-06-10T13:49:18Z","email":"dmytro.denysov@danads.se","name":"Dmytro Denysov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-06-10T13:49:18Z","email":"dmytro.denysov@danads.se","name":"Dmytro Denysov"},"message":"The code introduces a query bus implementation using Symfony Messenger, along with necessary interfaces and abstract classes for queries and query handlers.  Additionally, it integrates Hateoas for hypermedia support in the user service, and adds a new route and controller for handling a `FindPingQuery`.\n\nHere''s a breakdown of the changes and some suggestions:\n\n**Key Changes:**\n\n*   **Query Bus Implementation:**  The core library (`libs/core`) now has a `QueryBusInterface`, `AbstractQuery`, `QueryInterface`, `QueryHandlerInterface`, and a Symfony Messenger-based implementation (`MessengerQueryBus`).  This allows dispatching queries to handlers via the message bus.\n*   **Query Handling:** The user service (`services/user-service`) defines a `FindPingQuery` and its corresponding handler `FindPingQueryHandler`. The handler retrieves data from the data store based on the query.\n*   **HTTP Delivery:** A new `ViewController` is added to the user service. This controller transforms an HTTP request into a `FindPingQuery`, dispatches it, and uses Hateoas to serialize the result before returning a JSON response.\n*   **Hateoas Integration:**  The `willdurand/hateoas` library is added to the user service''s dependencies, along with Symfony''s `serializer` and `property-info` components, likely required by Hateoas.\n*   **Routing:** A new `/view` route is added to the user service, mapping to the `ViewController`.\n*   **Request Transformation:** A `RequestToQueryTransformer` is introduced in the core library to convert Symfony HTTP requests into query objects.\n\n**Suggestions and Potential Improvements:**\n\n1.  **Query Class Properties:** In `AbstractQuery` and `FindPingQuery`, the `id` property is defined.  Consider adding type hints (e.g., `public string $id;`) for better type safety and code clarity.  If `id` is not always required, you could make it nullable (`?string $id`).\n\n2.  **RequestToQueryTransformer:** The `RequestToQueryTransformer::transform` method currently instantiates a `FindPingQuery` directly, regardless of the `$queryClass` argument. This should be changed to instantiate the class provided by `$queryClass`  (e.g.,  `return new $queryClass($attrs);`).  Also, add validation to ensure that the query parameters match the expected properties of the query class, potentially throwing an exception if there are mismatches.\n\n    ```php\n    // ... inside RequestToQueryTransformer::transform\n\n    $attrs = [];\n    $query = new $queryClass(); // Instantiate the correct class\n    $vars = array_keys(get_class_vars($queryClass));\n\n    foreach ($vars as $var) {\n        if (!isset($queryParams[$var])) {\n            continue;\n        }\n        $attrs[$var] = $queryParams[$var];\n    }\n\n    return new $queryClass($attrs);\n    ```\n\n3.  **Error Handling:**  The `ViewController` doesn''t have specific error handling.  Consider adding try-catch blocks to handle potential exceptions during query dispatch or serialization, and return appropriate HTTP error responses (e.g., 400 for invalid input, 500 for server errors).\n\n4.  **Hateoas Configuration:** The Hateoas builder is used in the controller, but there''s no configuration for how resources should be represented (links, embedded resources, etc.).  You''ll need to define resource configurations (likely through annotations, XML, or YAML) to actually leverage Hateoas'' hypermedia features.  Without configurations, it will just serialize the data.  For example, you might create a `config/serializer/` directory and add a `FindPingQuery.yml` file:\n\n    ```yaml\n    # config/serializer/FindPingQuery.yml\n    Denysov\\UserService\\Application\\Query\\FindPingQuery:\n        exclusion_policy: ALL # or NONE, depending on which properties you want to expose\n        properties:\n            id:\n                expose: true\n            # other properties to expose\n        links:\n            - rel: self\n              href:\n                  route: view # Assuming ''view'' is the route name for getting a single ping\n                  parameters:\n                      id: expr(object.id)\n    ```\n\n    Then, in your controller, tell Hateoas to use this configuration:\n\n   ```php\n    $hateoas = HateoasBuilder::create()\n        ->setMetadataDirectories([''Denysov\\UserService\\Application\\Query'' => __DIR__ . ''/../../config/serializer'']) // Adjust path as needed\n        ->build();\n   ```\n\n5. **Return Type Consistency:**  The `MessengerQueryBus::dispatch` method enforces that handlers return an array.  While this might be suitable for this specific case, consider if a more flexible return type (e.g., an object representing the query result) would be beneficial in the future.  You could update the interface and implementation accordingly if needed.\n\n6. **FindPingQuery - ID only?** The `FindPingQuery` currently only has an `id` property. If you intend to add more query parameters in the future, define them explicitly as properties in the class. This ensures type safety and clear parameter handling.\n\n7. **Read Model Users:** In `FindPingQueryHandler`, the collection name ''read_model_users'' is hardcoded.  Consider making this configurable, perhaps by injecting it into the handler or defining it as a constant.  This improves flexibility if the collection name changes.\n\n8. **Controller Naming:** The `ViewController` is named a bit generically.  A more descriptive name, like `FindPingController` or `PingViewController`, would improve code readability.\n\nBy implementing these suggestions, you can improve the robustness, maintainability, and clarity of your query bus implementation and Hateoas integration.","tree":{"sha":"0fb9c01174884f19e5d9d803e2d7bb722201bed7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/git/trees/0fb9c01174884f19e5d9d803e2d7bb722201bed7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/git/commits/5bc9c0218170c59e1e2500511b9fbfc59cbd9694","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/ddenysov/canope/commit/5bc9c0218170c59e1e2500511b9fbfc59cbd9694","node_id":"C_kwDOO2zci9oAKDViYzljMDIxODE3MGM1OWUxZTI1MDA1MTFiOWZiZmM1OWNiZDk2OTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ddenysov/canope/commit/d40b2694b97c396e1ece710c0700f429e784e5cd","sha":"d40b2694b97c396e1ece710c0700f429e784e5cd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/commits/d40b2694b97c396e1ece710c0700f429e784e5cd"}],"sha":"5bc9c0218170c59e1e2500511b9fbfc59cbd9694","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/commits/5bc9c0218170c59e1e2500511b9fbfc59cbd9694"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/commits/d40b2694b97c396e1ece710c0700f429e784e5cd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-06-10T06:41:52Z","email":"dmytro.denysov@danads.se","name":"Dmytro Denysov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-06-10T06:41:52Z","email":"dmytro.denysov@danads.se","name":"Dmytro Denysov"},"message":"The code change in `libs/core/src/Validator/ValidationResult.php` corrects the logic of the `valid()` function.  The original code incorrectly returned `true` if there were any errors, while the corrected code now returns `true` only if there are no errors (i.e., the count of errors is 0). This aligns with the expected behavior of a `valid()` function.","tree":{"sha":"67e8f2df1f27d2f4b11c882e3101e9035d116192","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/git/trees/67e8f2df1f27d2f4b11c882e3101e9035d116192"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/git/commits/d40b2694b97c396e1ece710c0700f429e784e5cd","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/ddenysov/canope/commit/d40b2694b97c396e1ece710c0700f429e784e5cd","node_id":"C_kwDOO2zci9oAKGQ0MGIyNjk0Yjk3YzM5NmUxZWNlNzEwYzA3MDBmNDI5ZTc4NGU1Y2Q","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ddenysov/canope/commit/33135c7a3732bac7d10fa11f9ae8c9c237314a8c","sha":"33135c7a3732bac7d10fa11f9ae8c9c237314a8c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/commits/33135c7a3732bac7d10fa11f9ae8c9c237314a8c"}],"sha":"d40b2694b97c396e1ece710c0700f429e784e5cd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/commits/d40b2694b97c396e1ece710c0700f429e784e5cd"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/commits/33135c7a3732bac7d10fa11f9ae8c9c237314a8c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-06-06T15:26:22Z","email":"dmytro.denysov@danads.se","name":"Dmytro Denysov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-06-06T15:26:22Z","email":"dmytro.denysov@danads.se","name":"Dmytro Denysov"},"message":"The code change in `libs/core/src/Validator/ValidationResult.php` corrects the logic of the `valid()` function.  The original code incorrectly returned `true` if there were any errors, while the corrected code now returns `true` only if there are no errors (i.e., the count of errors is 0). This aligns with the expected behavior of a `valid()` function.","tree":{"sha":"2e51bef709ead92aca05774c091f0ddc128fc057","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/git/trees/2e51bef709ead92aca05774c091f0ddc128fc057"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/git/commits/33135c7a3732bac7d10fa11f9ae8c9c237314a8c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/ddenysov/canope/commit/33135c7a3732bac7d10fa11f9ae8c9c237314a8c","node_id":"C_kwDOO2zci9oAKDMzMTM1YzdhMzczMmJhYzdkMTBmYTExZjlhZThjOWMyMzczMTRhOGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ddenysov/canope/commit/b355c3e6877064aae56aa1e02b005ea4a3a27fb6","sha":"b355c3e6877064aae56aa1e02b005ea4a3a27fb6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/commits/b355c3e6877064aae56aa1e02b005ea4a3a27fb6"}],"sha":"33135c7a3732bac7d10fa11f9ae8c9c237314a8c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/commits/33135c7a3732bac7d10fa11f9ae8c9c237314a8c"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/commits/b355c3e6877064aae56aa1e02b005ea4a3a27fb6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-06-06T15:22:11Z","email":"dmytro.denysov@danads.se","name":"Dmytro Denysov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-06-06T15:22:11Z","email":"dmytro.denysov@danads.se","name":"Dmytro Denysov"},"message":"The code introduces a command validation mechanism using Symfony''s validator component. Here''s a breakdown of the changes and potential improvements:\n\n**Key Changes:**\n\n*   **Command Validation:** A new `CommandValidator` class is created to handle command validation using Symfony''s `ValidatorInterface`. It checks for violations and returns a `ValidationResult` object containing the status code and any validation errors.\n*   **Validation Result:** The `ValidationResult` class stores the validation status (success/failure) and any associated error messages.\n*   **Command Interface:** An `AbstractCommand` class is introduced, providing a base implementation for commands, including automatic attribute assignment from an array and a `toArray` method.\n*   **Integration:** The `SymfonyCoreBundle` is updated to register the `CommandValidator` as a service.\n*   **Usage in Controller:** In the `IndexController`, the `CommandValidator` is used to validate a `PingCommand`. If validation fails, errors are returned in the JSON response. The command now takes an `id` and `firstName` from the request.\n\n**Code Review and Suggestions:**\n\n1.  **`JobsWorker.php`:**\n    *   The change `new $class(PingId::create())` to `new $class()` seems to imply that the `PingId` is no longer required or handled differently.  It might be helpful to add a comment explaining why this change was made.  Also, consider if `PingId` is still used elsewhere and if it can be removed completely.\n\n2.  **`docker-compose.yml`:**\n    *   The addition of port `8280:8080` exposes the user service on port 8280 of the host machine.  This is fine, but ensure this port doesn''t conflict with other services and that it aligns with the intended development workflow.\n\n3.  **`CommandValidator.php`:**\n    *   The status code 422 is appropriate for validation errors, but consider using constants or a more descriptive way to represent the status code (e.g., an enum or a constant in the `ValidationResult` class).\n\n4.  **`SymfonyCoreBundle.php`:**\n    *   The service registration for `CommandValidatorInterface` is correct.\n\n5.  **`ValidationResult.php`:**\n    *   The `valid()` method is incorrectly implemented. It should return `true` if the validation is successful (no errors) and `false` otherwise.  Currently, it returns `true` if there are errors.  **This needs to be fixed.**\n\n    ```php\n    public function valid(): bool\n    {\n        return count($this->errors) === 0;\n    }\n    ```\n\n6.  **`PingCommand.php`:**\n    *   The `PingCommand` now correctly extends `AbstractCommand`. Consider adding validation constraints (e.g., using Symfony''s validation annotations) to the `firstName` property to enforce rules like required, minimum length, etc.\n\n7.  **`AbstractCommand.php`:**\n    *   The constructor iterates through `$attributes` and assigns them to the command object''s properties. This is a good pattern. The `id` property is initialized, but it''s not clear where or how this is being set initially. It appears it''s set in the controller, but consider if this should be handled within the command itself or during command creation for consistency.\n    *   You could add type hinting to the `$attributes` parameter in the constructor for clarity (e.g., `array $attributes = []`).\n\n8.  **`IndexController.php`:**\n    *   The controller now retrieves `firstName` from the request and passes it to the `PingCommand` constructor. This is good.\n    *   The `Uuid::create()->toString()` generates a UUID for the command ID.  This is a good practice for ensuring unique command IDs.\n    *   The logic for handling validation results is correct, but it relies on the incorrect `valid()` method in `ValidationResult`.  Once that''s fixed, this will work as intended.\n    *   The response includes `violations`, `data`, and `firstName`.  Ensure this response structure meets the API''s requirements.\n\n**Overall:**\n\nThe code introduces a well-structured command validation system.  However, the incorrect implementation of the `valid()` method in `ValidationResult` needs to be addressed.  Also consider adding validation constraints to the `PingCommand` and clarifying how the command ID is managed for better consistency and robustness.","tree":{"sha":"f107fc0fbf84d85f8588e13f3dd511a28f301577","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/git/trees/f107fc0fbf84d85f8588e13f3dd511a28f301577"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/git/commits/b355c3e6877064aae56aa1e02b005ea4a3a27fb6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/ddenysov/canope/commit/b355c3e6877064aae56aa1e02b005ea4a3a27fb6","node_id":"C_kwDOO2zci9oAKGIzNTVjM2U2ODc3MDY0YWFlNTZhYTFlMDJiMDA1ZWE0YTNhMjdmYjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ddenysov/canope/commit/bb873af94ec0e5040dab7cbaadf4f9d483683bd1","sha":"bb873af94ec0e5040dab7cbaadf4f9d483683bd1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/commits/bb873af94ec0e5040dab7cbaadf4f9d483683bd1"}],"sha":"b355c3e6877064aae56aa1e02b005ea4a3a27fb6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/commits/b355c3e6877064aae56aa1e02b005ea4a3a27fb6"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/commits/bb873af94ec0e5040dab7cbaadf4f9d483683bd1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-06-06T09:15:45Z","email":"dmytro.denysov@danads.se","name":"Dmytro Denysov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-06-06T09:15:45Z","email":"dmytro.denysov@danads.se","name":"Dmytro Denysov"},"message":"The code changes how validation errors are formatted. Instead of a flat array of strings, it now organizes errors by field, making it easier to associate errors with specific input fields.\n\nHere''s a breakdown:\n\n*   **Original:** Errors were stored as strings like `\"fieldName: Error message\"`.\n*   **Modified:** Errors are now stored in an associative array where the key is the field name and the value is an array of error messages for that field.  For example: `[\"fieldName\" => [\"Error message 1\", \"Error message 2\"]]`.\n\nThis change improves the structure of the error output, which is beneficial for displaying errors in a user-friendly manner (e.g., next to the relevant form fields).  However, it changes the format of the error output, which might require adjustments in how the client-side handles errors.","tree":{"sha":"1827355261655e161fadc4f24d2c4ce4ff782df4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/git/trees/1827355261655e161fadc4f24d2c4ce4ff782df4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/git/commits/bb873af94ec0e5040dab7cbaadf4f9d483683bd1","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/ddenysov/canope/commit/bb873af94ec0e5040dab7cbaadf4f9d483683bd1","node_id":"C_kwDOO2zci9oAKGJiODczYWY5NGVjMGU1MDQwZGFiN2NiYWFkZjRmOWQ0ODM2ODNiZDE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ddenysov/canope/commit/67b2f1b328cad56aa3e36bac131bc12c1d723317","sha":"67b2f1b328cad56aa3e36bac131bc12c1d723317","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/commits/67b2f1b328cad56aa3e36bac131bc12c1d723317"}],"sha":"bb873af94ec0e5040dab7cbaadf4f9d483683bd1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/commits/bb873af94ec0e5040dab7cbaadf4f9d483683bd1"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/commits/67b2f1b328cad56aa3e36bac131bc12c1d723317/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-06-06T09:12:56Z","email":"dmytro.denysov@danads.se","name":"Dmytro Denysov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-06-06T09:12:56Z","email":"dmytro.denysov@danads.se","name":"Dmytro Denysov"},"message":"The changes introduce a Traefik reverse proxy setup for the `user-service` application. Here''s a breakdown:\n\n*   **`services/user-service/docker-compose.yml`**: The `user-service` container is now integrated with Traefik.  It''s exposed on port 8080 internally, connected to an `intranet` network, and labeled for Traefik to route requests with the `/users` prefix to it.  A middleware is configured to strip the `/users` prefix before forwarding the request to the application.\n\n*   **`gateway/config/traefik_static.yml`**: This new file defines the Traefik entrypoint `web` listening on port 8000 and enables the Traefik dashboard for monitoring.\n\n*   **`gateway/Makefile`**: This new file provides convenient commands for managing the gateway service (start, stop, restart, ssh).\n\n*   **`gateway/docker-compose.yml`**: This new file defines the Traefik service. It uses the official Traefik image, configures it to listen on port 8000, exposes ports 8000 and 8081 (for the dashboard), connects to the `intranet` network, and mounts the Docker socket to allow Traefik to dynamically discover and configure routes for other services.\n\n**Potential Improvements:**\n\n*   **Security:** Exposing the Traefik dashboard (`--api.insecure=true`) without authentication is a security risk.  In a production environment, you should secure the dashboard with authentication (e.g., HTTP Basic Auth) or disable it entirely.  Consider adding Traefik configuration to enable authentication for the dashboard.\n\n*   **Network Creation:** The `intranet` network is defined as `external: true` in both `docker-compose.yml` files.  This implies the network should be created separately using `docker network create intranet`.  It might be more convenient to define the network creation within one of the `docker-compose.yml` files (e.g., in the gateway''s file) to ensure it exists.  For example, in `gateway/docker-compose.yml`, you could define the network as:\n\n    ```yaml\n    networks:\n      intranet:\n        driver: bridge\n    ```\n\n    This way, the network will be automatically created when you bring up the gateway service.\n\n*   **Makefile:**  The `gateway/Makefile` is well-structured for basic operations.  You might add a `logs` command to follow the Traefik logs for easier debugging:\n\n    ```makefile\n    logs:\n    \tdocker compose logs -f traefik\n    ```\n\n*   **Error Handling:** Consider adding error handling or checks within the `Makefile` commands to improve robustness. For instance, checking if commands succeed or providing more informative messages.\n\n*   **Comments:** While the comments are present, consider adding more comments to explain complex configurations, especially within the Traefik static configuration file, explaining the purpose of each setting.\n\n**Example of secure dashboard (in `gateway/docker-compose.yml`):**\n\nTo secure the dashboard, you''d need to configure an HTTP Basic Auth middleware and apply it to the dashboard route.  Here''s how you''d modify `gateway/docker-compose.yml` (and you would remove `--api.insecure=true`):\n\n```yaml\nservices:\n  traefik:\n    image: traefik:v2.11\n    command:\n      - \"--api.dashboard=true\"\n      - \"--providers.docker=true\"\n      - \"--entrypoints.web.address=:8000\"\n      - \"--entrypoints.traefik.address=:8080\" # Add this for secure dashboard access\n    ports:\n      - \"8000:8000\"\n      - \"8081:8080\"\n    networks:\n      - intranet\n    volumes:\n      - \"/var/run/docker.sock:/var/run/docker.sock:ro\"\n      - \"./config:/etc/traefik\" # Mount a config directory\n    labels:\n      - \"traefik.http.routers.traefik.rule=Host(`traefik.localhost`)\" # Route to dashboard\n      - \"traefik.http.routers.traefik.service=api@internal\"\n      - \"traefik.http.routers.traefik.entrypoints=traefik\" # Use the secure entrypoint\n      - \"traefik.http.routers.traefik.middlewares=traefik-auth\" # Apply authentication\n      - \"traefik.http.middlewares.traefik-auth.basicauth.users=admin:$$apr1$$lKVd8t8.$$oF7.e8oM8Q64N6n5K.b3g1\" # Replace with actual hashed credentials\n\nnetworks:\n  intranet:\n    external: true\n```\n\nYou''d also need to modify `gateway/config/traefik_static.yml` to remove the insecure API access and configure the `traefik` entrypoint:\n\n```yaml\nentryPoints:\n  web:\n    address: \":8000\"\n  traefik: # Add this entrypoint for dashboard access\n    address: \":8080\"\n\n# No more api section\n```\n\nRemember to replace the dummy credentials in the `docker-compose.yml` with your actual hashed credentials.  You can generate the hash using `htpasswd`. Now, the dashboard would be accessible on `traefik.localhost:8081` (assuming you''ve configured your hosts file to resolve `traefik.localhost` to your Docker host''s IP).","tree":{"sha":"7501f00fa60dc30f6612a5dfa971a4d32722615a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/git/trees/7501f00fa60dc30f6612a5dfa971a4d32722615a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/git/commits/67b2f1b328cad56aa3e36bac131bc12c1d723317","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/ddenysov/canope/commit/67b2f1b328cad56aa3e36bac131bc12c1d723317","node_id":"C_kwDOO2zci9oAKDY3YjJmMWIzMjhjYWQ1NmFhM2UzNmJhYzEzMWJjMTJjMWQ3MjMzMTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ddenysov/canope/commit/13f13b77aed2c48f54eae71b6146be217534de10","sha":"13f13b77aed2c48f54eae71b6146be217534de10","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/commits/13f13b77aed2c48f54eae71b6146be217534de10"}],"sha":"67b2f1b328cad56aa3e36bac131bc12c1d723317","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/commits/67b2f1b328cad56aa3e36bac131bc12c1d723317"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ddenysov/canope/commits/13f13b77aed2c48f54eae71b6146be217534de10/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-06-06T08:31:42Z","email":"dmytro.denysov@danads.