://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/827634?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akelmanson/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akelmanson/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akelmanson/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akelmanson/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/akelmanson","id":827634,"login":"akelmanson","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgyNzYzNA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akelmanson/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akelmanson/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akelmanson/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akelmanson/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akelmanson/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akelmanson","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/callstackincubator/react-native-sandbox/commits/b6ccdc6e691653c223e2c98ea5fae3d25ffccc24/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-29T20:22:28Z","email":"akelmanson@gmail.com","name":"akelmanson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-29T20:22:28Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(android): touch interceptor must ignore pointerEvents none/box-none (#39)\n\n`SandboxTouchInterceptor.isObscuredAt` decided whether a sandbox is covered by\nan overlay using only the sibling''s visibility + bounds — it never checked\n`pointerEvents`. React Native''s AppContainer adds a full-screen\n`pointerEvents=\"box-none\"` overlay in dev (LogBox / the element inspector),\ndrawn on top of everything. That overlay was treated as obscuring, so every\ntouch landing in a sandbox was rerouted via `redispatchWithHiddenSandbox` and\nthe sandbox became untappable — but only in debug builds (release has no such\noverlay), which makes it very easy to miss.\n\nFix: skip siblings whose `pointerEvents` is NONE (fully transparent to touch),\nand skip the own-bounds test for BOX_NONE (its own box passes touch through;\nonly its children can catch). Descendant checks are unchanged.\n\nFollow-up to #33 (the interceptor introduced there).\n\nCo-authored-by: André Kelmanson <andre@grana.capital>","tree":{"sha":"8b6c002f53c9ccbb67495a66e805458a6d973bc9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/callstackincubator/react-native-sandbox/git/trees/8b6c002f53c9ccbb67495a66e805458a6d973bc9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/callstackincubator/react-native-sandbox/git/commits/b6ccdc6e691653c223e2c98ea5fae3d25ffccc24","verification":{"payload":"tree 8b6c002f53c9ccbb67495a66e805458a6d973bc9\nparent c7cc802c002ed95ac4e5c688ab5ebe6a7a2e3711\nauthor akelmanson <akelmanson@gmail.com> 1782764548 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782764548 +0200\n\nfix(android): touch interceptor must ignore pointerEvents none/box-none (#39)\n\n`SandboxTouchInterceptor.isObscuredAt` decided whether a sandbox is covered by\nan overlay using only the sibling''s visibility + bounds — it never checked\n`pointerEvents`. React Native''s AppContainer adds a full-screen\n`pointerEvents=\"box-none\"` overlay in dev (LogBox / the element inspector),\ndrawn on top of everything. That overlay was treated as obscuring, so every\ntouch landing in a sandbox was rerouted via `redispatchWithHiddenSandbox` and\nthe sandbox became untappable — but only in debug builds (release has no such\noverlay), which makes it very easy to miss.\n\nFix: skip siblings whose `pointerEvents` is NONE (fully transparent to touch),\nand skip the own-bounds test for BOX_NONE (its own box passes touch through;\nonly its children can catch). Descendant checks are unchanged.\n\nFollow-up to #33 (the interceptor introduced there).\n\nCo-authored-by: André Kelmanson <andre@grana.capital>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqQtQECRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAV20QAFV3Gq6ymUdZIb0+/npz+R0C\nYlb4L7CdIKRE3Lmay