x an issue with the filtering of order types in the Order details table that is outlined [here](https://openmrs.atlassian.net/browse/O3-4419). Specifically, this PR:\n\n- Changes the `orderType` parameter in the order types fetch request API URL  to `orderTypes`.\n- Fixes the range date click handler logic to properly deal with timezone differences.\n- Rename `orders-details-table` to `order-details-table` for consistency.\n- Add type assertions and improve test data completeness.\n\nCo-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"56f00bc9c486bea1baa23c339647f2e2c7e08289","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nurazizUGM-Intero5/OpenMRS-Module-Patient/git/trees/56f00bc9c486bea1baa23c339647f2e2c7e08289"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nurazizUGM-Intero5/OpenMRS-Module-Patient/git/commits/24cd98ccb5662f5fbfce4675d81db2a2c1fa96ec","verification":{"payload":"tree 56f00bc9c486bea1baa23c339647f2e2c7e08289\nparent 8e5314d48be6a036cf9b670a877f257cc7b6a8ce\nauthor praneeth <praneeth7077@gmail.com> 1745444443 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1745444443 +0300\n\n(fix) O3-4419: Fix order type filtering in order details table (#2385)\n\nThis PR attempts to fix an issue with the filtering of order types in the Order details table that is outlined [here](https://openmrs.atlassian.net/browse/O3-4419). Specifically, this PR:\n\n- Changes the `orderType` parameter in the order types fetch request API URL  to `orderTypes`.\n- Fixes the range date click handler logic to properly deal with timezone differences.\n- Rename `orders-details-table` to `order-details-table` for consistency.\n- Add type assertions and improve test data completeness.\n\nCo-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJoCV5bCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA2X0QAGbUJ/eBBFuWERbTolwJPASq\nn/QLoEtC4MR/K+CBvzqMYLqhsDo2wChkZp+bJehi63Lx3rr8eCqnu541H8bcvJhb\n4kB/y1H+lbsksUDlakeyT02XfB9caMrS+UqqLIn49ylZDNi/47UVXElY2O55CW9o\